# SRG-APP-000149-AU-002280  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must use multifactor authentication for network
# access to privileged user accounts.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000149-AU-002280
group:           V-206461
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000765
control_rev5:    IA-2

contribution:    Splunk Web can require a client certificate and use it as the user
                 credential, which carries the DoD PKI factor the requirement prefers for
                 network logon; the product's alternative route is the Duo or RSA
                 integration in authentication.conf (externalTwoFactorAuthVendor with
                 externalTwoFactorAuthSettings), and an instance configured that way meets
                 the same application share by that route instead of the two conditions
                 below.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] requireClientCert equals true
check:           web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth equals true
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] requireClientCert https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Issuance, validity and possession of the DoD PKI credential, and the card
                 reader and middleware on the client machine
external:        Where the organization uses Duo or RSA instead of PKI, the vendor's
                 enrollment and policy decide whether the second factor is actually
                 demanded of each privileged account
external:        Privileged access over SSH or the host console is authenticated by the
                 operating system, not by Splunk

citation:        SRG-APP-000149-AU-002280 check and fix text ("DoD PKI or another
                 multifactor authentication method"); web.conf.spec:120-132
                 (enableCertBasedUserAuth, default false, requires requireClientCert true),
                 web.conf.spec:151-167 (requireClientCert, default false);
                 authentication.conf.spec:87-99 (externalTwoFactorAuthVendor supports Duo
                 and RSA, no default)
finding:         Splunk requires no second authentication factor for network logon by
                 privileged accounts: neither the certificate path (web.conf
                 requireClientCert and enableCertBasedUserAuth both true) nor the vendor
                 path (authentication.conf externalTwoFactorAuthVendor with
                 externalTwoFactorAuthSettings) is configured.
